      <div>
        <h2 id="also-title">Also on the platform</h2>
        <p class="lede">The credit case is the argument. These are the systems that made it possible to run one source of truth.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="also-grid">
      <div>
        <h3>One platform, one source of truth</h3>
        <p>Consolidated an in-house operations app, an Odoo instance and a sprawl of spreadsheet trackers into a single Frappe/ERPNext platform covering field operations, records and finance.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Offline-first field workflows</h3>
        <p>Built for field officers across low-connectivity districts after ride-alongs showed the product, not the training, was the problem. Leadership had been ready to go back to spreadsheets. An offline MVP kept the system: over 80% of transactions now captured on-device, data lag from days to same-day.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Weighted-average-cost procurement</h3>
        <p>Landed cost computed continuously and surfaced at the point of decision, moving deal go/no-go from days to same-day across a multi-party supply chain.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Discovery, not internal opinion</h3>
        <p>Ride-alongs with agriculture officers, farmer interviews, a 36-role inventory of everyone who touches the systems, and staged pilots before any wider release. A farmer asked for pictures of urea and DAP instead of labels; the interface followed that, not the copy we had written in the office.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>HR, payroll and finance for 300+ people</h3>
        <p>HRMS live 1 July 2025: attendance, leave and policy in the workflow instead of email and spreadsheets. Payroll preparation from about three days to about an hour. Petty cash across 17 locations, and more than a hundred travel requests a month on tracked approvals.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

